{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments ["<b>His young men</b> — He compared the consuming of the sword to the consuming of fire, in the manner of: \"For a fire went out from Heshbon.\" And the sense of the vav in בחוריו — for the death of the pious in war." "<b>And his virgins</b> — that they were modest; they did not see wedding canopies upon the death of the young men."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "Resolved the unnamed biblical quotation in the second clause as Numbers 21:28 by its distinctive wording; the first clause quotes Psalms 78:63 itself."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:21.392637619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}